WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.790
- [Narrator] Before Donald
Trump became president

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.179
he was better known for this.

00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:07.560
- You're fired. You're
fired. You're fired.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.660
- Donald Trump was known
through and through

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.380
as a New Yorker, a businessman,
a socialite, essentially.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.450
- [Narrator] That reputation
is now at the center

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.670
of Trump's civil fraud trial in Manhattan

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.280
where he and his adult
children face allegations

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.560
that they falsify the
value of their assets

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.930
for millions in ill-gotten gains.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.940
- This is a rare scenario

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.540
where you have a case of
this financial significance

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.060
with a player of this public visibility

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.580
and involving so much Real Estate

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.730
of so many assets in New York.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.530
- [Narrator] Here's how
Trump's civil fraud trial

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.590
could deal a blow to the former
president's New York empire

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.300
and the business titan persona

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.433
he's built over the course of decades.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.000
Trump faces four criminal indictments

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.460
related to his time as
president, but for him,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.220
the civil fraud case in
Manhattan Court is personal.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.370
- This could have
potentially crippling effects

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.400
on Donald Trump's business
interest in New York

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.020
and the Trump organization's ability

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:05.700
to continue to do business in New York.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.490
He spent decades pursuing business deals

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.433
across the city, residential, commercial.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.640
- [Narrator] In a 2022 lawsuit

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.490
New York Attorney General
Letitia James, accused Trump

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.000
and his adult children, of
engaging in a decade-long scheme

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.910
to fraudulently and
falsely value their assets

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:28.110
resulting in $250 million
in unlawful gains.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.690
James, a Democrat and
a vocal critic of Trump

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.750
alleges the former president
was able to obtain bank loans

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.293
on more favorable terms, by
overvaluing his Real Estate.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.540
These properties include

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.210
Trump's flagship Manhattan
building, Trump Tower

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.280
an office building
known as 40 Wall Street,

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.440
the residential building Trump Park Avenue

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.510
and in an estate north of New York City

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.280
known as Seven Springs.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.620
- Cases like this are not rare

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.250
but this is one of the most unusual ones

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:00.420
because of the high profile
identity of the person involved.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.840
The fact that it involves
substantial number of properties

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.960
with high values in New York.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:07.830
- [Narrator] The lawsuit said

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.810
the triplex apartment in Trump Tower

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.270
was calculated at 30,000 square feet,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.390
when in reality it's
nearly 11,000 square feet.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.390
That resulted in a valuation
of $327 million in 2015

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.290
more than triple the record setting price

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.860
for any apartment ever sold
in the city at that point.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.240
And at Trump Park Avenue,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.030
the lawsuit claimed 12
rent stabilized units

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.330
were appraised at $750,000 total.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.900
According to Trump's financial
statements in 2011 and 2012

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.660
those units were valued as
if they were unrestricted

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.863
for nearly $50 million.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.570
- In the law, there is no bright line

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:50.430
between what constitutes a
reasonable, perhaps exaggeration

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.380
but when you get to the point

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.033
where the statement of
value is so many multiples,

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.620
10, 20, 100 times,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.320
what would be shown to
be the actual value,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.740
a judge or jury can draw
the conclusion if he wishes

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.973
and it would be justified
that this is a fraud.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.670
- [Narrator] Trump has
denied any wrongdoing

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.500
and called the case a witch hunt.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.660
His lawyers have argued
that his business dealings

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.210
have been profitable
for the banks involved.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.860
- The banks got back their money.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.910
Again, there was never a
default. It was never a problem.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.030
Everything was perfect.
There was no crime.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.040
- [Narrator] In the early
proceedings before the trial

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.720
a New York judge ruled that Trump

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.520
and two of his adult children

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.850
Eric Trump and Donald
Trump Jr. committed fraud.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.220
Both Donald Trump Jr. and Eric Trump

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.450
have criticized the ruling

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.970
saying they relied on
the company's accountants

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.670
to compile their father's
financial statements.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.800
Ivanka Trump was dismissed from the case

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.120
after an appeals court ruled

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.180
the state's legal claims
against her were too old.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.580
In September, the judge
ordered the cancellation

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.650
of business certificates that allow Trump

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.570
to operate in the state,
which could lead him

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.840
to lose control of some
New York properties.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.240
- You can't just take assets from somebody

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.560
without compensation.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.990
If this goes forward,
there has to be a process

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.630
which is certainly fair
to the defendant, to Trump

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:13.440
to realize the proper
value of those assets.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.000
Whether or not that Trump name

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.060
is gonna come off the buildings,
is very much intertwined

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.120
with what is the way to
realize the most value

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.043
if those assets are sold.

00:04:24.432 --> 00:04:26.670
- [Reporter] Trump, how's it going today?

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.290
- Trump is not hiding at all

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.900
his displeasure with his entire process.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.600
- This is a case that should
have never been brought.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.415
It's a case that should
be dismissed immediately.

00:04:36.415 --> 00:04:38.970
The fraud was on behalf of the court.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.220
- [Narrator] The Attorney
General wants to prohibit Trump

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.690
and his company from entering

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.240
into New York State commercial
Real Estate acquisitions

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.670
and applying for loans with
state registered lenders

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.320
for five years.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.680
In early January, James
said Trump and his company

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.010
should pay about $370 million in penalties

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:59.400
more than the $250 million
she originally estimated

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.410
for their ill-gotten gains.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.510
- There's a lot of questions
of where Trump would get

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.030
the cash freed up to satisfy that.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.690
One possibility is he would
have to sell some properties off

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.110
or other assets to free
up that amount of cash.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.820
- [Narrator] In October, an appeals court

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.860
temporarily postponed the cancellation

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.480
of Trump's business certificates

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.940
while his lawyers contested the ruling.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.550
- The irony here is if this goes forward

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.480
and Trump is no longer involved,
the very thing that he says

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:30.540
would lend extraordinary value
to these properties beyond,

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.270
for example, the appraisal
values, would haunt him

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.700
because these properties
would no longer have

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:39.300
the Trump brand and the
values that would be realized

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.120
one would think would
be substantially lower.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.410
- [Narrator] Some legal experts

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.510
say Trump's lawyers
seem focused on building

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:48.000
a detailed legal record for an appeal.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.080
- The appellate road is
long and it is not quick.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.360
And if we consider where we are now,

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.730
I think that the scale tips heavily

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.270
in favor of the Trump
Organization, in being able to

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.360
delay any final resolution of this case

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.910
until after the next
presidential election.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.960
- Politically, Trump has so
far, used this and the other

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.810
legal travails that he
faces to paint himself

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.090
as a victim of political persecution.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:18.330
In a lot of ways it's worked
with Republican core voters,

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.570
but a loss could turn the tables on that

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:24.090
some of his legal problems could compound

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.090
and he could be hurt in the face of voters

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.537
as he tries to return to the White House.

00:06:29.537 --> 00:06:32.120
(gentle music)

